---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import RoofLookup from "../components/RoofLookup.astro";
import {
  totalDetections,
  highConfidence,
  perBuildingPolygons,
  citiesWithDetections,
  surveyGeneratedDate,
  crossDomainRegions,
} from "../data/stats";
import { electricityRate, monthLabel } from "../data/tariff";

// What the reader gets, kept out of the hero so the hero holds four text
// elements at most and the address field reaches the top of a phone screen.
const deliverables = [
  { label: "satellite view", detail: "your rooftop at building resolution" },
  { label: "system size", detail: "usable roof area converted to kWp" },
  { label: "payback", detail: "years, priced at your own bill" },
  { label: "permit", detail: "cost range and the DOE fast-track clock" },
  { label: "neighbours", detail: "rooftop solar already detected on your block" },
];
---
<Base title="SolarMap.PH · what can your roof do?" pathname="/" description="Type your address and SolarMap.PH measures your roof from satellite, sizes a solar system in kWp, estimates payback against your Meralco bill, and shows detected rooftop solar near you. Free, no signup.">
  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 pt-10 md:pt-14 pb-6">
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[1.05] mb-4 text-ink-900 font-semibold tracking-tight max-w-2xl">
      What can your roof do?
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-ink-700 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
      Type your address. We measure your actual roof from satellite and tell you whether solar pays back.
    </p>
  </section>

  <RoofLookup />

  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 mt-12 reveal">
    <ul class="grid gap-px bg-ink-300/30 border border-ink-300/30 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5">
      {deliverables.map((d) => (
        <li class="bg-paper p-4">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink-900 mb-1">{d.label}</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 leading-snug">{d.detail}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 leading-relaxed mt-4 max-w-3xl">
      Free, no signup. SolarMap.PH runs no backend. The address you type goes straight from your browser
      to third-party geocoders (Photon, Nominatim, Overpass, Esri tiles, PVGIS) and never reaches a
      server we control. <a href="/privacy" class="no-underline text-accent-steel">What gets seen by whom &rarr;</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-14 mt-8 border-t border-ink-300/30 reveal">
    <div class="max-w-prose">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-5 leading-tight">Three asymmetries decide whether a Filipino homeowner gets a fair solar deal.</h2>
      <p class="text-base text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Installer quotes vary 5x for the same system. LGU permit fees range ₱16K-153K for the same project.
        Net metering caps residential export at 100 kW, targets a 10-working-day utility decision, and
        depends on a 3-day LGU fast-track that many LGUs have not adopted. Neutral information is hard to come by.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        This tool reads your address, finds your building in OpenStreetMap, measures the roof from satellite,
        runs the payback math at the {monthLabel(electricityRate.as_of)} Meralco residential rate of
        ₱{electricityRate.php_per_kwh.toFixed(4)}/kWh, and says what to do next. It also shows nearby rooftops
        where our computer-vision survey already detected solar, and the local permit cost where we could verify it.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
        No installer pays to be recommended. No data leaves your browser. The math is open-source and reproducible.
        <a href="/methodology" class="no-underline text-accent-steel">How we computed everything &rarr;</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 pb-16 grid gap-px bg-ink-300/30 md:grid-cols-[1.15fr_1fr] border border-ink-300/30 reveal">
    <a href="/map" class="bg-paper p-6 md:p-8 no-underline group transition-colors hover:bg-paper-alt">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono mb-3">research backplane</p>
      <h2 class="text-xl mb-4 text-ink-900">{totalDetections} rooftops with detected solar across {citiesWithDetections} cities</h2>
      <dl class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-4 border-y border-ink-300/30 py-3">
        <div>
          <dt class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono">high-confidence</dt>
          <dd class="text-2xl font-mono tabular-nums text-ink-900">{highConfidence}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono">per-roof polygons</dt>
          <dd class="text-2xl font-mono tabular-nums text-ink-900">{perBuildingPolygons}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono">extra regions</dt>
          <dd class="text-2xl font-mono tabular-nums text-ink-900">{crossDomainRegions}</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
        Detections score above 0.85, calibrated to 96% precision on the held-out NCR validation set.
        The {crossDomainRegions} franchises outside Metro Manila carry their own per-domain calibration
        or ship as candidate inventory with no precision claim. Survey generated {surveyGeneratedDate}.
      </p>
      <span class="text-sm font-medium text-accent-steel group-hover:text-ink-900">Open the map &rarr;</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/methodology" class="bg-paper p-6 md:p-8 no-underline group transition-colors hover:bg-paper-alt">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-ink-500 font-mono mb-3">how it works</p>
      <h2 class="text-xl mb-4 text-ink-900">A frozen CLIP encoder, a calibrated head, then SAM for the panel outlines</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        How the model was trained, calibrated and validated: the active-learning rounds, the encoder
        ablation, the per-domain calibration that replaced an over-optimistic cross-region precision, and
        the segmentation step that turns a tile-level score into a per-building panel polygon.
      </p>
      <span class="text-sm font-medium text-accent-steel group-hover:text-ink-900">Read methodology &rarr;</span>
    </a>
  </section>
</Base>
